# Pinned REFERENCE model for the numerical-correctness gate (§1 golden parity + §2
# tuned-vs-generic on a stable model). This is intentionally SEPARATE from the deploy-
# specific SMOKE_MODEL (which varies per release, e.g. a PGO build points it at the
# deployed quant): the golden vectors in golden.tsv are tied to THIS exact file, so it
# must stay fixed. Changing it is a fixture change — regenerate golden.tsv with
# scripts/gen-golden.sh (and update the sha here).
#
# Suggested: bge-small-en-v1.5 Q8_0 (the small BERT embedding model bge-small consumers
# use downstream). Fail-closed: correctness.sh requires both to be non-empty.
#
# The `:-` defaults let CI override via repo variables (vars.CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL /
# vars.CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256) without editing this file; the values here are the
# canonical in-repo pin. correctness.sh fails closed if the sha is empty from both.
#
# REQUIRED before the gate goes live: fill in the real sha256 (curl the URL, run
# `sha256sum`) — either here or as the repo variable — and regenerate golden.tsv with
# scripts/gen-golden.sh against the same file.
CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL="${CORRECTNESS_MODEL_URL:-https://huggingface.co/CompendiumLabs/bge-small-en-v1.5-gguf/resolve/main/bge-small-en-v1.5-q8_0.gguf}"
CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256="${CORRECTNESS_MODEL_SHA256:-}"
